speechtext:
1. Yes; departed December 3, 1965, returned December 7, 1965; The guest list was as follows: V. A. Ainsworth, president, Newfoundland Board of Trade; J. D. Allingham, manager, Allingham's Travel Agency; R. Armitage, assistant manager, Maritime Transportation Commission; W. S. Bird, chairman, New Brunswick Development Corporation; Hon. C. H. Ballam, Minister of Labour, government of Newfoundland and Labrador; R. Bassett, manager, Bermuda Trade Development Board; R. MacD. Black, publisher, Amherst Daily News; J. Braddock, managing editor, Atlantic Advocate; J. Bray ley, bureau chief, Canadian Press; F. Brooks, manager, Maritime Travel Service; S. Bujold, managing director, L'Evangeline; J. V. Butler, president, VOCM radio; G. C. Cherry, Cherry's Travel Service; W. H. Conrod, photographer; R. Costello, president, Telegraph-Journal and Times Globe;

R. Crawford, Fundy Shipping Limited; W. V. Creaghan, president, Moncton Board of Trade; G. A. Cromwell, general manager, CHSJ Radio and Television; J. M. Crosby, chairman, Maritime Transportation Commission; L. C. Currie, publisher, Daily News;
R.	E. Day, Guy R. Day and Son; J. H. Delaney, United Mine Workers of America; M. Doogue, manager, Annapolis Valley Travel Service; R. D. Duchemin, publisher, Cape Breton Post; L. C. Earle, director, Harvey's Travel Agency; F. Fillmore, freelance; W. W. Fowler, regional sales manager, Air Canada; A. Frampton, president, Central Newfoundland Chamber of Commerce; D. Frost, manager, Central Agencies; W. F. Galgay, regional director, Canadian Broadcasting Corporation; A. W. Gaudet, president, Charlottetown Board of Trade; G. C. Goode, regional operations manager, Air Canada; W. J. Hancox, publisher, Guardian and Patriot; H. S. Haslam, general manager, coal operations, Dominion Steel Corporation; J. M. Herder, president, The Evening Telegram; H. Holland, president, Stephenville Chamber of Commerce; B. W. Isner, general manager, Times and Transcript; C. Jamieson, general manager, CJON Radio and Television; E. G. Jarvis, president, Halifax Board of Trade; R. A. Kellough, manager, Blenus Travel Service;
S.	R. Kennedy, regional director, Canadian Broadcasting Corporation; A. J. Kenny, manager, Harvey's Travel Agency; H. J. Lam, manager, Atlantic Travel Service; J. A. Lenahan, regional controller, Department of Transport; R. V. Lenihan, manager, Moncton Travel Agency; C. Linkletter, Linkletter Travel Agency; R. Lockhart, managing director, CFBC Radio; F. A. Lynds, president, CKCW Radio and Television; A. B. MacDonald, president, Sydney Board of Trade; F. MacDonald, president, CJCH Limited; G. A. MacDonald, freelance; R. MacDonald, J. A. Young and Son; D. Macintosh, vice president, Fraser and Hoyt Travel Service; I. Mac-Keigan, chairman, Atlantic Development Board; J. G. McFarlane, manager, Harvey's Travel Agency; Hon. A. B. MacRae, Minister of Agriculture, Province of Prince Edward Island; W. J. McCall, city editor, Halifax Herald; G. R. McGregor, president, Air Canada; W. McKay, general manager, The Western Star; J. L. McKenna, president, Canadian Weekly Newspapers Association; F. McQuarrie, president, Summerside Board of Trade; E. R. Mathers, manager, I. H. Mathers and Son Limited; J. W. E. Mingo, chairman of the port of Halifax commission; R. S. Morton,
February 2, 1966

publisher, Dartmouth Free Press; D. Mosley, manager, H. D. MacLeod Agency Limited; J. Mungall, publisher, Journal-Pioneer; C. N. Murray, general manager, steel operation, Dominion Steel Corporation; J. Murphy, president, Truro Daily News; Dr. N. Murphy, president, CFCB Radio; D. M. Neill, president, CFNB Radio; J. O'Dea, president, Atlantic Provinces Economic Council; V. DeB. Oland, past president, Canadian Chamber of Commerce; P. A. Outhit, freelance writer; A.
T.	Parkes, secretary manager, Maritime Provinces Board of Trade; W. L Patterson, sales manager, CFDR Radio; O. Pulsifer, assistant manager, CHNS Radio; A. Purchase, president, Corner Brook Chamber of Commerce; J. R. B. Rankin, area manager, public relations, Air Canada; G. Regan, barrister; B. Richard, Acadia Travel Agency; J. A. Rioux, president, Fredericton Board of Trade; H. D. Robertson, manager, Robertson Travel Limited; Hon. H. J. Robichaud, Minister of Fisheries, government of Canada; C. Robinson, maritime editor, Weekend magazine; S. Rodriguez, manager, Atlas Travel Service; K. A. Ross, general manager, Halifax Board of Trade; P. Sampson, Bathurst Travel Bureau; R. C. Schurman, president, CJRW Radio; I. Schwartz, president, Glace Bay Travel Service; Warden I. Settle, municipality of the county of Halifax; D. Sheppard, president, Gander Chamber of Commerce; F. G. Sher-ratt, general manager, Radio CJCH 920 Ltd.; J. G. Simpson, director, Air Canada; Hon. R. L. Stanfield, Premier of Nova Scotia; C. M. Sullivan, president, Saint John Board of Trade; J. R. H. Sutherland, publisher, New Glasgow News; N. Swain, manager, South Shore Travel Service; G. Theriault, station manager, CBAF Television; G. T. Urquhart, chairman, Port and Industrial Commission; Mayor Charles A. Vaughan of Halifax; Mayor Joseph Zatzman of Dartmouth, Nova Scotia.
2.	The Hon. H. J. Robichaud and Mr. G. Regan, former member of parliament (see answer to number one) were among those on the inaugural flight.
3.	The president of Air Canada or his office did not make available a certain number of seats on said flight to the Minister of Transport. Hon. H. J. Robichaud represented the Minister of Transport on the flight and the Minister of Transport suggested to Air Canada that an invitation be extended to Mr. I. M. MacKeigan as chairman of the Atlantic Development Board and to Mr. G. Regan, since Mr. Regan had been the first and most persistent advocate in parliament of the Halifax-Bermuda Service.
